               \\\"score\\\": 22,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Grounded in the source's bridge between analyzer output and source-level transformations.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-lina-kovac\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"The reported loop-bound results are impressive, especially 707 loops with 99% analyzability and 96% exactness. For hard real-time work, automating that many flow facts matters almost as much as the later optimizations, because manual loop annotations are exactly where safety and productivity can both suffer.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 23,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses specific evidence and connects it to real-time development concerns.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-4\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-rory-chen\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"I would be cautious about generalizing the speedups beyond the WCC, aiT, and TriCore setting. The matmult reduction from 775,720 to 227,794 cycles is a strong demonstration of composition, but the result depends on the target architecture, benchmark behavior, and the analyzer/compiler integration being mature.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 25,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Balances strong quantitative evidence with the source's stated scope limitations.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-5\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-samira-haddad\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"The register-allocation result is a good example of optimizing the right thing for real-time systems. Avoiding spills on the worst-case execution path may increase text size, but that trade-off is sensible when the contract is about a safe upper bound rather than average throughput.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 21,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Clearly reflects the WCET-aware register allocation trade-off described in the source.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\noutput_path.write_text(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + '\\\\n', encoding='utf-8')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
